# The doc-tools commit this platform pairs with. It is read by
# .github/workflows/cross-repo-kind-drift.yml, which runs doc-tools' overlay drift test at this
# commit against this tree's policy/overlays.
#
# Bump it when a release note pairs the platform with a new doc-tools release, in the same commit
# as the note. A pin that lags the pairing measures drift against a doc-tools nobody deploys.
# Bump it ALSO in the same commit as any overlay `passes` change: doc-tools owns passes and the
# overlay mirrors them (architect, 2026-10-24), so a mirrored row is only checkable against a
# doc-tools that declares it.
#
# Currently doc-tools #172's head at 12eed082 (2026-10-30), NOT main and NOT a release. It is the
# only doc-tools commit that declares structural.outline on `course`, and #172's own CI needs this
# overlay row, so each side pins the other's commit. The `main` leg reds until #172 merges: that is
# the report doing its job. Move this onto doc-tools main when #172 merges, and back onto a release
# when doc-tools tags one.
12eed082b3552296cc18706ae022a755136893a1
